## register rows for the 42 assigned requirements (status, final_gate, acceptance, notes)

### REQ-PB-093 status=IMPLEMENTED final_gate=DG5
ACCEPTANCE: A06;A07: an admin changes the default Feasibility rubric text and the default weights to 30/20/20/15/15 in the UI and publishes without a code change; a transformation created afterwards starts with the new default; an existing transformation keeps its weight set and rubric version; publishing defaults that total 95% is rejected
NOTES: Playbook (B0077): weights are adjusted to the transformation context. Master-prompt additions (§9 M0176; §6 M0154, M0155): scoring rubrics and approved weights are configurable and versioned, administered in Playbook Studio with draft, publish and version pinning; the source weights 25/25/20/15/15 are seeded (M0176, REQ-PB-048). Interpretations: that seed is the initial Studio default for new transformations, and ADM configures defaults only, never approving a transformation's weights (permissions-matrix.md §5 rule 2). AN-05: split from REQ-PB-049 (finding F-DG0-001). DG5 analyst check (T-DG5-AN-P5A, base f78afff): scoring-defaults.test.ts, a06-configuration-change.test.ts and a07-historical-integrity.test.ts assert that a changed Feasibility rubric and weights 30/20/20/15/15 reach only transformations created afterwards, that an existing transformation keeps 25/25/20/15/15 and rubric v1, and that 95% is refused (422 config_version.weights_total); partly covered in the UI: p5-studio.spec.ts publishes a scoring-defaults version through the Studio screens but changes one rubric descriptor only, and the 30 entry with exact decimal totals is a studio.test.tsx component test, so the exact 30/20/20/15/15 browser path is not driven end to end.

